From 944d358b7613250cbbfe903ba79ae6dcd4991bdd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mavis Agent <agent@mavis.local>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 04:23:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] The visitor counter: Umami on this box, same-origin, no
 cookie

How many people the site brings and where they came from, counted on our
own server and nowhere else.

  * deploy/analytics-install.sh installs Umami + PostgreSQL in Docker,
    both bound to 127.0.0.1 - the dashboard is not on the internet and is
    reached through an SSH tunnel;
  * it creates the website and writes /var/www/plivariverlodge/analytics.js
    with the website id. The id is NOT committed;
  * nginx serves /stats.js and /api/send from THIS domain, so the
    visitor's browser never talks to a third party and no cookie is set;
  * index.html loads the tracker with one line. If the file is not there
    the browser gets a 404 and nothing else on the page is affected;
  * deploy/ANALYTICS.md compares Umami with Google Analytics,
    Cloudflare and Statcounter, and says why GA is the wrong one here
    (cookie banner, the data leaves the country, and it cannot say which
    Facebook group sent the visitor).

The tracker workbook builds the posting link with a utm_campaign tag, so
the answer to "which group sent this visitor" is in the data.

